{
 "_comment": "Issue #159 part B's anti-drift guard, updated for the movement rules (wide rivers and mountains impassable to land armies, a stream - any river tile that is not wide - walkable at a flat 1.0 + RiverCrossingCost = 9.0 whatever terrain it runs over). HexPathfinderGoldenTests.cs (backend) and hexPath.golden.test.ts (frontend) both compute against this fixture using each side's OWN production cost tables and wide-river rule (RiverArms.cs / riverArms.ts, from the full river tiles below), then assert the frozen results. Either side's cost model drifting from the other turns its own suite red, instead of the client's range tint quietly disagreeing with what the server actually paths over. Generated by scripts/regen-goldens/river-pathing-golden.ts from the frontend pathfinder; never hand-edit. walls are the standing palisade hexes (an army with case.army 'friendly' belongs to the wall owner, 'enemy' to anyone else; the default is friendly): every wall hex blocks, a gate passes only its owner's armies, a land end with one wall neighbour that touches no mountain or wide river is half open and costs the ground plus 3.0 (HexPathfinder.HalfOpenEndCost / HALF_OPEN_END_COST). bridges are the bridge hexes (a level-0 foundation opens nothing; the bridges and the walls share one owner, an army with case.army 'friend' belongs to another owner who is that owner's friend): levels 1 and 2 cost 1.0 + 5.0 and 1.0 + 3.0 for every army, levels 3 and 4 cost 1.0 + 0.5 (the ground under the river never sets the price), level 4 for the owner and friends only (HexPathfinder.CausewayCrossingCost / FootbridgeCrossingCost / KingsBridgeCrossingCost, BridgeIndex.cs; bridgeMovement.ts). terrain omits sea - any (q, r) not listed is sea (impassable to a land unit). A case with expectedPath null has no route. hexesPerHour/speedFactor are always 1.0 in these cases so every hour figure below is a plain sum of step costs. A step is billed half and half: (leave price of the hex left + enter price of the hex entered) / 2 - the leave price is the enter price, except that a wall built under the army does not shut the hex it stands on and a wide river with no bridge costs 1.0 + 11.0 = 12 to leave (HexPathfinder.BurntBridgeLeaveCost).",
